        "paragraphs": [
            "SpaceXAI Grok is the model family from the developer xAI. The pages describe Grok models for chat, coding, reasoning, and knowledge work, along with related lines such as Grok Build for coding, Grok Bot for always-on agents, Grok Imagine for image and video, and Grok Voice for speech. The family has grown from Grok-1.5 and the Grok-2 and Grok-2 mini beta models through Grok 3 and Grok 3 mini to later releases including Grok 4.5, Grok 4.6, and Grok 4.7. xAI says Grok 4.7 is its most powerful model for coding and knowledge work, and it describes Grok 4.6 as building on Grok 4.5 with a focus on long-running agents and more ambitious interactive and visual work.",
            "xAI offers Grok through the SpaceXAI API, where usage-based pricing starts from $2 per million tokens and the newest flagship is grok-4.7 with a 500k context window. The API covers text and code generation, image and video generation and editing, voice agents, and live web and X search, and it works with existing SDKs in Python, TypeScript, or curl. xAI also provides a Console with a Playground, API keys, and billing, and an enterprise API that adds SSO, audit logging, invoicing, data residency, and dedicated support. Grok models are additionally available through cloud platforms including Microsoft Azure, Oracle, and Google Cloud, and through products such as GitHub Copilot, Amazon Bedrock, and Microsoft Foundry."
        ],
